If a peaceful is invisible and you can't see invisible, iirc moving
into its square counts as an attack.

However, these conditions are hard to meet.
Usually peaceful monsters are not invisible, since they only zap /oI
or quaff !oI if you can see invisible. The exception (which iirc has
happened to me) is that you quaffed a !oSI or wore a =3DSI, the
peaceful monster used !oI or /oI, and when you lost See Invisible
intrinsic you can no longer see the peaceful. As an example, you
could be testing non-cursed rings on a shop, trying a =3DSI and the
shopkeeper becoming invisible: if you do not buy the ring getting
out of the shop without angering the shopkeeper can be tricky.

